{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Behaviour vectors for the gesture engine (python: bollardeck.device.gestures, js: bollardeck.gestures). Each vector makes a fresh engine from \"config\" and feeds it \"events\" in order. An event is a button edge (down, up or cancel, with a button), a tick, a key event (edge \"key\": \"key\" holds a device key event, and t_ms is when it is read, passed as now_ms) or a change of combos (edge \"combos\", with \"combos\"), at t_ms. \"emits\" lists the gestures that very call must return, in order, each with the time it became certain; an emitted gesture may also state \"hold_ms\", how long its press lasted, which must then match. An event with no \"emits\" must return none. \"raises\": true means the call must fail and the vector ends there. Every timeline is made up.",
  "vectors": [
    {"name": "tap-on-a-button-without-combos", "about": "Button 2 has no combos: its tap is reported at the release.", "config": {"hold_ms": 800, "tap_follow_ms": 500, "combos": {"1": [3], "3": [3]}}, "events": [
